# Controller scratch — never commit, never touch except the task report file.
#
# GR6 gr6-120: the review PROSE is the exception, and it is the exception
# because ignoring it caused a blocker. The final whole-branch review's sixteen
# findings and its adjudication table were declared an input to the grand
# review's triage; they lived only inside a task's output text; and this line —
# ignoring the entire directory — meant `git show` could not recover them. The
# queue stalled on a document that technically existed nowhere.
#
# So: every `.md` under `.superpowers/sdd/` is tracked (findings, backlogs,
# reviews — the durable record of why the tree looks the way it does), and
# everything else under `.superpowers/` stays ignored: `worktrees/` above all,
# which holds N full working copies of this repository, plus session state,
# screenshots and probe output. The re-ignore below is load-bearing — an
# un-ignored `**/*.md` would otherwise sweep in every agent worktree's own
# copy of every markdown file in the tree.
.superpowers/**
!.superpowers/sdd/
!.superpowers/sdd/**/
!.superpowers/sdd/**/*.md
# Belt and braces: a worktree under either scratch root is a full copy of this
# repository, so an un-ignored `**/*.md` would otherwise sweep in every agent's
# copy of every markdown file in the tree.
.superpowers/**/worktrees/

# Agent scratch — worktrees, session state, local agent config
.claude/
